ajar: /tmp/nosuch.jar: No such path or directory.

### ajar x of a damaged entry
ajar c0Mf /tmp/a.jar data/words.txt && sed 's/quick/QUICK/' /tmp/a.jar > /tmp/b.jar && mkdir /tmp/out && cd /tmp/out && ajar xf /tmp/b.jar; echo "status $?"
--- out
status 1
--- err
ajar: data/words.txt: The data does not match its check value.

### ajar a missing file
ajar cMf /tmp/a.jar data/nosuch data/fruits.txt; echo "status $?"; ajar tf /tmp/a.jar
--- out
status 1
data/fruits.txt
--- err
ajar: data/nosuch: No such path or directory.

### ajar archives read by pax are refused
ajar cMf /tmp/a.jar data/fruits.txt && pax -f /tmp/a.jar; echo "status $?"
--- out
status 1
--- err
pax: The input is not an archive in a known format.
